|rarity = RR
|name1 = Maize Cat
|name2 = Cone Cat
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Cone Cat''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
Maize Cat is an extremely useful specialist meatshield, sharing many similarities with [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]], its Anti-Angel equivalent. A level 30 Maize Cat has '''74.8k''' effective health against Relic and Aku, with further boosts against Colossal threats of these traits like [[Zero Luza]] and [[Omens]]. It also has immunity to curse and freeze, which actually improves its potency as a meatshield quite a lot as a surprising number of Relic and Aku enemies have the freeze ability, while curse immunity is obviously important for any short ranged anti-Relic unit. The main difference in usage between Maize Cat and Ramen Cat is that its high speed makes it easier to protect distant units, but it can't maintain a thick line of defense and therefore cannot be your only source of protection, even with the help of [[Cat Combo]]s such as [[Biohazard (Combo)|Biohazard]] and [[Bony Bone (Combo)|Bony Bone]] as they'll all just rush forward, whereas the likes of [[Primordial Cat (Rare Cat)|Future Cat]] don't tend to wander far. This means it's best to use Maize Cat with another meatshield like [[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Rock Cat]] or [[Manic Eraser Cat|Manic Eraser]] for better defense.

The main downside to Maize Cat is its hefty cost of 375, which is quite high for a spammable meatshield. This doesn't necessarily make it a cash drain, but spamming it may make it harder to save money for more expensive cats. It also lacks immunity to surges and status effects, which makes it vulnerable to Aku threats in general and the likes of [[M. Ost|M. Ost]]. All in all, Maize Cat is a very potent meatshield against its targeted traits, making it a welcome addition to your team.

