==Trivia==
*Maize Cat's design and walking animation are very similar to the maize-dog hybrid [https://prcdn.freetls.fastly.net/release_image/36495/479/36495-479-647e9c8f2eb0c7eb8ff11aa42b4c15db-3900x3605.png?format=jpeg&auto=webp&quality=85%2C65&width=1950&height=1350&fit=bounds Wankōn] (わんコーン, "Wancorn") from one of [[PONOS Corporation|PONOS]]' other games, [https://web.archive.org/web/20260514172222/https://www.ponos.jp/games/no-longer-momotaro/ No Longer MOMOTARO] (桃太郎失格). Cone Cat also has a similar Japanese name: Nyankōn (にゃんコーン, "Nyancorn" or "Nyancone"), which is ''Wankōn'' with ''nyan'' (meow) instead of ''wan'' (woof). No Longer MOMOTARO was released January 17th, 2022, only 7 months before Version 12.6 added Maize Cat to [[Nyanko Daisensou|BCJP]] (August 23rd, 2022).
*Maize Cat's evolution into Cone Cat may play off of how コーン ''kōn'' can mean "corn" or "cone", as well as the fact that corn byproducts in real life can be processed for further applications, sometimes replacing plastic items for environmental concerns.

